# Festag Night — dark mode tokens

Canonical source: `lib/design-tokens/dark.ts` → applied in `app/globals.css` `[data-theme="dark"]`.

## Ladder

| Layer | Token | Value |
|---|---|---|
| Canvas | `--festag-black-canvas` | `#000000` |
| Content | `--festag-black-content` | `#0D0D10` |
| Raised | `--festag-black-raised` | `#151518` |
| Popup | `--festag-black-popup` | `#1B1B20` |
| Peak | `--festag-black-peak` | `#232328` |
| Ink | `--festag-night-ink` | `#E4E4EA` |

## Rules

1. Prefer tokens over hardcoded `#0c0c0e` / `#111114` / `#121214` / `#FFFFFF` in dark UI.
2. Soft ink (`#E4E4EA`) — not pure white body text (glare).
3. Soft cool-white primary CTAs (`#F0F2F5`) in portal; auth idle stays quiet slate.
4. Quiet hairlines (`--festag-night-line` ~6.5% white) — not loud strokes.
5. Desaturated semantics (`#4BC98E` / `#C9A45C` / `#D97272` / `#6BA8E8`).
6. No frosted glass blur on OLED — glass tokens remap to opaque elevation.
7. Fallbacks in `var(--token, #hex)` must match Festag Night hexes.

## Do not

- Reintroduce pure `#FFFFFF` as default dark body text
- Fork a second black ladder in auth/Tagro/popup (inherit from html)
- Use neon greens/blues for status dots
